{"id":"608600880","kind":"article","title":"原子记忆","author":"Piotr Wozniak","original_authors":["Piotr Wozniak"],"original_source_urls":["https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Atomic_memory"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2023-02-22","updated":"2023-02-22","votes":11,"comment_count":0,"minutes":1,"chars":649,"keywords":["原子记忆","间隔重复","最小信息原则","记忆复杂性","记忆稳定性"],"summary":"术语条目把“原子记忆”定义为最简单概念间的联想，并说明作者为何主张间隔重复巩固这类单位：它们可组合表示复杂知识，长期维持成本较低。条目还以苹果识别和词语联结对比复杂、简单记忆，解释复杂项目的概念激活可能不完整且顺序不稳，呼应最小信息原则。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/608600880","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"0P_Ch82R\"><b>原子记忆</b>是记忆中最简的概念之间的联想，是最低<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Complexity\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">复杂度</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>的记忆。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Spaced_repetition\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>倡导巩固这种<b>原子记忆</b>，因为不费力，而且也可以用来表示任意<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Complexity\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">复杂度</a>的知识。有一点很重要，即如果一组知识能用一组原子记忆表示，那么维持所有这些原子记忆的长期记忆的成本，比维持一部分原始记忆的成本，都会小很多。虽然原子记忆的遗忘是指数级的，但是相比于复合记忆，这种遗忘的下降常数非常低。</p><p data-pid=\"rqBqPCvK\">人类记忆天然会简化外部世界的表示，得到简单的模型，以原子记忆存储。这样大脑就能低成本地记住复杂的世界，提高运算能力，也就获得更高的智能，更好的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Problem_solving\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">问题解决</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>能力。</p><figure data-size=\"normal\"><img class=\"origin_image zh-lightbox-thumb\" data-original-token=\"v2-70e6ee21101d699949b9c5dce5e95527\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-70e6ee21101d699949b9c5dce5e95527_r.jpg\" width=\"450\"/><figcaption>Memory complexity: simple and complex memories</figcaption></figure><p data-pid=\"5YLiwCpN\"> 图：<b><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Memory_complexity\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆复杂度</a></b><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>证明了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Minimum_information_principle\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">最小信息原则</a>的必要性。记忆简单的一问一答时，每次复习都能一致地唤起对应的问答对应关系。而对于复杂记忆，其概念的激活是不完全的，或者因上下文而变换顺序。因此，每次复习时，每个概念的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Memory_stability\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">记忆稳定性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>是无法统一增强的。复杂的项目难以记忆。虽然对于认出一个苹果，需要利用复杂的连接网络，但「apple」和「pomo」之间的联系是最简的。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"MYDWeeqn\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>感谢主要译者Shom、校对 <span class=\"nolink\">J</span>arrett Ye<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Atomic_memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Atomic memory - supermemo.guru</a><br/>本<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Glossary\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">术语表</a>条目用于解释 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo_Guru\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>，一位自 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/History_of_spaced_repetition_(print)\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">1987</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup> 年以来的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Spaced_repetition\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>软件先驱。</blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 记忆稳定性 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559298549\" href=\"#/post/559298549\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 间隔重复 (spaced repetition) <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"305651556\" href=\"#/post/305651556\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 如何解决任何问题？ <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"351779186\" href=\"#/post/351779186\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 记忆稳定性 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559298549\" href=\"#/post/559298549\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 什么是 SuperMemo <a href=\"https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/supermemo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/supermemo</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 0 目录《间隔重复的历史》 <a href=\"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/375379522\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/375379522</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"608391951","title":"我重塑大脑，使其精通数学","author":"Barbara Oakley","votes":1892,"minutes":12,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"612277299","title":"行为系统","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":40,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"351779186","title":"如何解决任何问题？","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":130,"minutes":40,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"304800091","title":"记忆复杂性","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":19,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"559298549","title":"记忆稳定性","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":11,"minutes":4,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"279166945","title":"间隔效应","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":21,"minutes":3,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「间隔重复」· Andy Matuschak"}],"rec_answers":[]}